# Caddy in front of Radio Remote. The app itself listens on 127.0.0.1:8080 only; Caddy is what the network sees.
# Why Caddy: browsers only allow the MICROPHONE on HTTPS pages. Without HTTPS you can listen but not talk.
#
# Caddy's reverse_proxy already forwards WebSockets and sets X-Forwarded-For / X-Forwarded-Proto, which the app
# trusts ONLY because the connection comes from 127.0.0.1. Never bind the app to 0.0.0.0 behind a proxy.

# --- Option A: LAN, Caddy's own certificate authority --------------------------------------------------------
# Each device must trust Caddy's root certificate once (see docs/06-security-remote.md).
raspberrypi.local {
	tls internal
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
}

# --- Option B: Tailscale name with a real, publicly trusted certificate ---------------------------------------
# Needs HTTPS enabled in the Tailscale admin console and Caddy allowed to talk to tailscaled
# (REQUIRES VERIFICATION on your install: Caddy's `get_certificate tailscale` support and permissions).
#
# raspberrypi.your-tailnet.ts.net {
# 	tls {
# 		get_certificate tailscale
# 	}
# 	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
# }
#
# If you add a hostname the app does not see in the Host header, list the browser origin in config:
#   [server] allowed_origins = ["https://raspberrypi.your-tailnet.ts.net"]
